SOURCE /Users/kevinkitanga/hermes/packs/claude-blog/skills/blog/templates/how-to-guide.md
1|# Template: How-To Guide
2|
3|**Template Name:** How-To Guide (Step-by-Step Tutorial)
4|**Target Word Count:** 2,000-2,500 words
5|**Description:** A structured, actionable tutorial that walks readers through a specific process from start to finish. Each step is concrete, visual, and builds on the previous one. Designed to rank for "how to" queries and earn featured snippets.
6|
7|## When to Use This Template
8|
9|- **Content Goals:** Drive organic traffic from instructional queries, establish topical authority, earn featured snippets for step-based queries
10|- **Search Intent:** Informational / Transactional hybrid: the reader has a specific problem and wants a clear solution *right now*
11|- **Best For:** Process explanations, software tutorials, setup guides, configuration walkthroughs, skill-building content
12|- **Avoid When:** The topic lacks a clear sequential process or has fewer than 3 meaningful steps
16|## Section-by-Section Structure
20|### Title (H1)
35|### Introduction (150-200 words)
60|### Prerequisites / Before You Begin (100-150 words)
65|- Required tools/software (with versions)
66|- Required accounts or access
83|### Step 1: [Action Verb] + [Specific Object] (200-300 words)
107|### Step 2: [Action Verb] + [Specific Object] (200-300 words)
117|### Step 3: [Action Verb] + [Specific Object] (200-300 words)
127|### Step 4: [Action Verb] + [Specific Object] (200-300 words)
139|### Step 5: [Action Verb] + [Specific Object] (200-300 words)
147|### Step 6: [Action Verb] + [Specific Object] (200-300 words)
159|### Common Mistakes to Avoid (150-200 words)
185|### Results / What Success Looks Like (100-150 words)
202|### Optional Reader Questions (count by reader need)
219|#### How long does it take to set up a CI/CD pipeline?
223|#### Can I use [Alternative Tool] instead?
227|#### What should I do if Step [N] fails?
231|#### How do I scale this for a larger team?
235|#### Is [Tool/Service] free?
241|### Conclusion with CTA (50-100 words)
252|## Template Checklist

SOURCE /Users/kevinkitanga/hermes/packs/claude-blog/skills/blog/templates/listicle.md
1|# Template: Listicle
2|
3|**Template Name:** Listicle (Ranked/Numbered List)
4|**Target Word Count:** 1,500-2,000 words
5|**Description:** A curated, opinionated list of tools, resources, strategies, or options ranked by quality or relevance. Each item gets a concise evaluation with clear "best for" positioning. Designed to rank for "best [X]" and "[N] top [Y]" queries, capture comparison traffic, and earn featured snippets for list-format results.
6|
7|## When to Use This Template
8|
9|- **Content Goals:** Capture high-volume "best of" search queries, provide quick decision-making support, drive affiliate or referral traffic, establish curation authority
10|- **Search Intent:** Commercial investigation: the reader is evaluating options and wants an expert-curated shortlist
11|- **Best For:** Tool roundups, resource collections, strategy compilations, product recommendations, tip collections
12|- **Avoid When:** The topic requires deep analysis of only 1-2 options (use the Comparison template instead) or the items cannot be meaningfully ranked or differentiated
16|## Section-by-Section Structure
20|### Title (H1)
37|### Introduction (100-150 words)
65|### Item 1: [Item Name] - Best Overall / Best for [Primary Use Case] (150-200 words)
102|### Item 2: [Item Name] - Best for [Specific Use Case] (150-200 words)
110|### Item 3: [Item Name] - Best for [Specific Use Case] (150-200 words)
120|### Item 4: [Item Name] - Best for [Specific Use Case] (150-200 words)
128|### Item 5: [Item Name] - Best for [Specific Use Case] (150-200 words)
138|### Items 6-N: [Continue as needed] (150-200 words each)
142|**Note:** Every item must earn its spot. If you can't write 150 meaningful words about an item, it doesn't belong on the list. Padding with filler items destroys credibility.
146|### Comparison Table (Feature Matrix)
152|**Required columns:**
167|### How We Selected These
204|### Optional Frequently Asked Questions
222|#### What is the best static site generator in 2026?
226|#### Is [Free Option] good enough for production?
230|#### What's the difference between [A] and [B]?
236|### Conclusion with Top Pick Recommendation (50-100 words)
248|## Template Checklist

